	(text "Seam board per spec §6 'Seam pogo'. Variants: 'left' (default; 2 x spring), 'right-left' (2 x flat),\n'right-right' (pair A, spring), 'numpad' (pair A, flat). Pogo halves are THT, hand-soldered; U701/U702 assembler-placed.\nPad 1 = spring S end / flat N end, so facing pads mate k <-> k: LA, LB, S1, S2 pass straight through like a USB-C cable.\nFlat seam boards mount flipped about the contact line relative to spring boards.\nTPD4E05U06 channel 1 on each pair's signals, channel 2 unused; no supply pin, so an unpowered module does not load the link.\nNo VBUS parts here: the link board's SMF6.0A (and KTS1693 upstream) protect it. J_SEAM pin order matches link J602;\ncable pin 1 to pin 1. Both halves share the SAMZO GA0480/GA0481 land pattern; flat variants override Value/MPN only."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 10.16 177.8 0.0000)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			) (justify left top)
		)
